p.src:
The four-component Dirac wavefunction satisfies $i\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial t}
=
-i\alpha_i\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial x_i}
+m\beta\Psi,
\qquad i=1,2,3,$ where a repeated spatial index is summed. Thus the derivative term means $\alpha_1\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial x}
+\alpha_2\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial y}
+\alpha_3\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial z}.$ For a plane wave this becomes the algebraic equation $\omega\Psi=(\alpha_i k_i+m\beta)\Psi.$

